      "pronunciationText": "Now read the slope at the other landmarks. At pi over two, the peak, the curve is flat, so the slope is zero. The curve is symmetric about that peak, so at pi it falls as steeply as it rose at zero. The slope there is minus one. At three pi over two, the trough, it's flat again: zero. And at two pi, the wave starts over, climbing with slope one. Peaks and troughs are flat, and the crossings are the steepest. On the wheel, the seat moves up or down fastest as it passes the hub's height, and for an instant it isn't climbing at all, at the top and the bottom."
    },
